# tzdata-style rule source - EDITION B (new / current ledger after the rename).
#
# Same DST clock rules as edition A, but the rename has landed: the old names
# Asia/Calcutta and Asia/Dacca are now links to the canonical zones instead of
# separately-accounted data zones. US/Eastern and US/Central stay links.
#
# Grammar is identical to rules_a_old.tzdata and parsed by the same reusable
# generator (factory/generator.rb).

ZONE America/New_York
OFFSET o1 -18000 0 EST
OFFSET o2 -18000 3600 EDT
TRANS 2024 3 o2 1710054000
TRANS 2024 11 o1 1730613600
TRANS 2025 3 o2 1741503600
TRANS 2025 11 o1 1762063200
TRANS 2026 3 o2 1772953200
TRANS 2026 11 o1 1793512800
TRANS 2027 3 o2 1805007600

ZONE America/Chicago
OFFSET o1 -21600 0 CST
OFFSET o2 -21600 3600 CDT
TRANS 2024 3 o2 1710057600
TRANS 2024 11 o1 1730617200
TRANS 2025 3 o2 1741507200
TRANS 2025 11 o1 1762066800
TRANS 2026 3 o2 1772956800
TRANS 2026 11 o1 1793516400
TRANS 2027 3 o2 1805011200

ZONE Europe/London
OFFSET o1 0 0 GMT
OFFSET o2 0 3600 BST
TRANS 2024 3 o2 1711846800
TRANS 2024 10 o1 1729990800
TRANS 2025 3 o2 1743296400
TRANS 2025 10 o1 1761440400
TRANS 2026 3 o2 1774746000
TRANS 2026 10 o1 1792890000
TRANS 2027 3 o2 1806195600

# Canonical South Asia zones remain data zones.
ZONE Asia/Kolkata
OFFSET o0 19800 0 IST

ZONE Asia/Dhaka
OFFSET o0 21600 0 +06

# Shared constant anchor carried by every cabinet (deduplicated block).
ZONE Etc/UTC
OFFSET o0 0 0 UTC

# The rename: old spellings are now aliases of the canonical zones.
LINK Asia/Calcutta Asia/Kolkata
LINK Asia/Dacca Asia/Dhaka

# Historical US aliases carried as links in both editions.
LINK US/Eastern America/New_York
LINK US/Central America/Chicago
